{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-019",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 19,
  "title": "Proverbs 19",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 19",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 19,
  "sortOrder": 20019,
  "verseCount": 29,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Better is the poor that walketh in his integrity, than he that is perverse in his lips, and is a fool.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Also, that the soul be without knowledge, it is not good; and he that hasteth with his feet sinneth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "The foolishness of man perverteth his way: and his heart fretteth against the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Wealth maketh many friends; but the poor is separated from his neighbour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "A false witness shall not be unpunished, and he that speaketh lies shall not escape.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Many will intreat the favour of the prince: and every man is a friend to him that giveth gifts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "All the brethren of the poor do hate him: how much more do his friends go far from him? he pursueth them with words, yet they are wanting to him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "He that getteth wisdom loveth his own soul: he that keepeth understanding shall find good.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "A false witness shall not be unpunished, and he that speaketh lies shall perish.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Delight is not seemly for a fool; much less for a servant to have rule over princes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "The discretion of a man deferreth his anger; and it is his glory to pass over a transgression.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "The king’s wrath is as the roaring of a lion; but his favour is as dew upon the grass.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "A foolish son is the calamity of his father: and the contentions of a wife are a continual dropping.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "House and riches are the inheritance of fathers: and a prudent wife is from the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Slothfulness casteth into a deep sleep; and an idle soul shall suffer hunger.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "He that keepeth the commandment keepeth his own soul; but he that despiseth his ways shall die.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He that hath pity upon the poor lendeth unto the LORD; and that which he hath given will he pay him again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Chasten thy son while there is hope, and let not thy soul spare for his crying.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "A man of great wrath shall suffer punishment: for if thou deliver him, yet thou must do it again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Hear counsel, and receive instruction, that thou mayest be wise in thy latter end.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "There are many devices in a man’s heart; nevertheless the counsel of the LORD, that shall stand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "The desire of a man is his kindness: and a poor man is better than a liar.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "The fear of the LORD tendeth to life: and he that hath it shall abide satisfied; he shall not be visited with evil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "A slothful man hideth his hand in his bosom, and will not so much as bring it to his mouth again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Smite a scorner, and the simple will beware: and reprove one that hath understanding, and he will understand knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "He that wasteth his father, and chaseth away his mother, is a son that causeth shame, and bringeth reproach.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "Cease, my son, to hear the instruction that causeth to err from the words of knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "An ungodly witness scorneth judgment: and the mouth of the wicked devoureth iniquity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:19:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "Judgments are prepared for scorners, and stripes for the back of fools.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 19:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:19:29"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
